<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX3-QA2-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX3-QA2-004" ;
  triage:title "AX.3 QA-2 re-assessment of AX3-013: admit()/transition() rejection message still omits the task id and the writer hand-rolls its own message instead of applying the pure functions (C6 one-application-site violation)" ;
  triage:description "AX.3 QA-2 (quality-mgr ax3-qa-r2, PR #1191 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T07:37Z; req-qa's C6 framing adopted over rust-qa-agent's minor rating) at head 116bd23b0. The pure state machine in crates/atm-storage/src/task_state.rs (admit()/transition()) still emits 'no open task for <actor>' without the task id, contrary to the spec text 'no open task <id> for <actor>', and a test asserts that stale contract. Production avoids the user-facing mismatch only because apply_task_completion in crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/writer/task_ops.rs hand-rolls its own correct message rather than applying admit()/transition() -- a second application site, violating the sprint's C6 'one application site' contract. Fix: make the rejection message carry the task id at the pure-function level (thread the id through the event or return a structured error the caller formats) and route the writer's missing-completion rejection through the single admit()/transition() path; update the test to the correct contract. Supersedes AX3-013's disposition (severity escalated from minor to important; does not edit AX3-013.ttl)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T09:06:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
